# Every file is checked out byte for byte as the repository holds it, whatever `core.autocrlf` of the machine says.
# A multi-line string literal holds the line breaks of its file, so a CRLF checkout changes what a program prints
# (tests/conformance/interpolation) and the C the compiler emits (the `agree` job of .github/workflows/gates.yml,
# which found both on the Windows runner, where Git converts to CRLF by default). The few files that are CRLF stay so.
* -text
